# Git push in NAS projects (Cursor / other windows)

When `git` is **not on PATH**, use GitHub Desktop’s Git by full path:

```powershell
$git = "C:\Users\bccli\AppData\Local\GitHubDesktop\app-3.5.4\resources\app\git\cmd\git.exe"
& $git status
& $git push origin <branch>
```

If the path doesn’t exist, check `C:\Users\bccli\AppData\Local\GitHubDesktop\` for the current `app-*\resources\app\git\cmd\git.exe`.

`phase-deploy.config.json` can set `gitExecutable` to this path so `npm run phase:deploy` works in any Cursor window.

Use **at most 10 git commands** per batch when scripting.
